diff --git a/AGENTS.md b/AGENTS.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..0497b30
--- /dev/null
+++ b/AGENTS.md
@@ -0,0 +1,43 @@
+# MesoVortexWX — Agent Notes
+
+Next.js (App Router) + React + MapLibre weather workstation. Map-first UI: a thin
+universal legend on top, compact top nav, a floating lower-left product panel, and a
+right-side warning drawer.
+
+## Commands
+
+- Dev server: `npm run dev` (serves on port 12000 in this environment)
+- Typecheck: `npx tsc --noEmit` (fast; use this as the primary gate)
+- `npx next lint` is very slow here — prefer `tsc` and spot-check lint when needed.
+
+## Data sources (all real; no placeholder data)
+
+- `app/api/lsr` — local storm reports (polls every 120s)
+- `app/api/spotter` — POST submits a spotter report; in-memory store, resets on restart
+- `app/api/weather/hyperlocal` — surface telemetry for a lat/lon (Open-Meteo, optional NWS station)
+- `app/api/weather-assistant` — Gemini-backed chat; needs `GEMINI_API_KEY` or returns 503
+- `lib/adapters/openmeteo.ts` — Open-Meteo forecast/minutely adapter
+- `lib/adapters/noaa.ts` — NWS alerts + latest station observation
+- `lib/adapters/weather-gateway.ts` — merges adapters into the hyperlocal telemetry shape
+
+## Gotchas learned
+
+- Open-Meteo `wind_speed_unit` accepts `kn` (not `knots`); the wrong value makes every
+  request 400 and silently degrades to fallback numbers.
+- Stull's wet-bulb formula is defined in Celsius — convert in and out.
+- Open-Meteo is location-addressed; an NWS station observation is only valid at that
+  station's own point, so never blend it into arbitrary coordinates.
+- Never return fabricated fallback observations; return `null` and surface an honest
+  "unavailable" state to the UI.
+- `public/service-worker.js` must be network-first for build assets, otherwise clients
+  get pinned to stale JS bundles across reloads and redeploys.
+- Default Gemini model: `models/gemini-2.5-flash` (match the sibling copilot route).
+
+## Environment notes
+
+- Downloads are served from `/workspace/downloads` on port 12001 (not 12000, which is
+  the Next dev server). Compact git bundle is built with
+  `git bundle create mvwx.bundle <branch> --not main` so it stays small and requires
+  `main` as a prerequisite.
+- Pushing to the GitHub remote may be blocked at the App permission level even when the
+  token reports push access; fall back to the bundle/patch download flow.
